{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And all these blessings shall come upon you and overtake you.</b> Even though you do not exert yourself to attain them." "<b>When you obey the voice of HaShem your Elohim.</b> And this is when your Torah is fixed and your occupation occasional; therefore the blessings will overtake you without exertion. Now he mentioned the blessings of the First Temple first, saying they will merit them at every time that they observe the commandments, until he said יְקִימְךָ ה׳ לוֹ לְעַם קָדוֹשׁ (Deuteronomy 28:9). And this was at the beginning of the Second Temple, as they of blessed memory recounted in the blessing upon the blessings of Shimon the Righteous and the miracles of the Temple all his days (Yoma 21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:23.971030809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}